 is a remote MCP server?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "An MCP server that runs on someone else's machine and is reached over HTTPS, so you add a URL instead of installing anything. Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and VS Code support them."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which public MCP server can I use for testing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Pick a read-only one from Documentation and knowledge or Weather, maps and travel: they need no input from you and cannot change anything. Check it first with our MCP Server Tester."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How many MCP servers need authentication?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "6,529 of the 20,778 endpoints we tested (31 %) answered with 401 or 403 or asked for a token, usually OAuth handled by your client."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How often is the list updated?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "This version is from 2026-10-26. We rerun the probe regularly; servers that stop answering drop out."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Shortform Kit", "item": "https://shortformkit.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Free Remote MCP Servers", "item": "https://shortformkit.com/free-remote-mcp-servers/"}]}</script>
