<p class="hint">Data: official MCP Registry, probed 2026-10-26, CC BY 4.0. Our own server, <a href="/mcp-server/">Shortform Kit</a> (social video transcripts, downloads and creator data), is in the full list like any other.</p></section>
  <section id="how" class="how"><h2>How it works</h2><ol><li><b>Pick a server</b> Browse the topics or download the full list.</li><li><b>Add it as a connector</b> Claude: Customize, Connectors, + Add, Add custom connector. Cursor, VS Code, Claude Code: see above.</li><li><b>Ask in plain words</b> Your assistant lists the server&#x27;s tools and calls them when they fit.</li></ol></section>
  
  
  <section id="faq" class="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Are there free remote MCP servers?</summary><p>Yes. In our test of 20,778 endpoints from the official MCP Registry, 11,903 answered without any API key or login. Picks by topic are on this page, the full list is a CSV download.</p></details><details><summary>What is a remote MCP server?</summary><p>An MCP server that runs on someone else&#x27;s machine and is reached over HTTPS, so you add a URL instead of installing anything. Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and VS Code support them.</p></details><details><summary>Which public MCP server can I use for testing?</summary><p>Pick a read-only one from Documentation and knowledge or Weather, maps and travel: they need no input from you and cannot change anything. Check it first with our MCP Server Tester.</p></details><details><summary>How many MCP servers need authentication?</summary><p>6,529 of the 20,778 endpoints we tested (31 %) answered with 401 or 403 or asked for a token, usually OAuth handled by your client.</p></details><details><summary>How often is the list updated?</summary><p>This version is from 2026-10-26. We rerun the probe regularly; servers that stop answering drop out.</p></details></section>
